/**
 * chatService.js
 * -------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * AI Counsellor Companion. Generates a reply that adapts tone according to
 * the selected personality and the emotion detected in the user's *current*
 * message (not a stale, previously-saved mood check-in).
 *
 * If AI_API_KEY is configured, replies are generated by OpenAI (default model
 * gpt-4o) using a counselling-grade system prompt: multilingual (replies in the
 * user's own language/script), personality-aware, with ~20 turns of memory and
 * model-side crisis detection in any language.
 * Otherwise, a template-based local responder produces a varied, message-
 * aware reply so the feature works with zero external configuration.
 *
 * Design notes on avoiding repetitive replies (this was a real bug, fixed
 * here): most everyday chat ("hi", "how are you", "thanks") carries no
 * strong emotional signal and classifies as "neutral". If the neutral-mood
 * templates are thin, or greetings get the same heavy "it sounds like
 * you're feeling..." framing as an emotional message, every casual message
 * ends up looking the same. This version:
 *   1. Detects greetings/small talk and answers them lightly and directly,
 *      without forcing mood-analysis language onto a "hi".
 *   2. Uses much larger variety pools (8-10 options) for openers,
 *      follow-ups, mood lines, and activity suggestions per mood.
 *   3. Uses independently-seeded hashes per component (not one shared seed)
 *      so two different messages essentially never produce an identical
 *      combination, even if they happen to share the same detected mood.
 *
 * Crisis-language messages always receive a fixed, safe, resource-pointing
 * response regardless of which backend is used (never left to the LLM).
 * -------------------------------------------------------------------------
 */

